title: "MK4: Frequency-Domain Biomarkers for Disease Detection"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-02-02
url: "https://github.com/Alexandria-dynamics/mk4-biomarker"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alexandria-dynamics/mk4-biomarker"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - biomarkers
  - disease-detection
  - RNA-seq
  - frequency-analysis
  - bioinformatics
  - transcriptional-chaos
  - risk-stratification
abstract: >
  MK4 is a frequency-domain biomarker framework for analyzing
  RNA expression data. It uses Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) and
  Shannon entropy to identify transcriptional chaos signatures
  associated with disease. Version 1.0 presents preliminary
  results for cancer, multiple sclerosis, and type 2 diabetes,
  with a validated negative control in Parkinson's disease.
  Key discoveries include the critical importance of dataset
  balance and the distinction between RNA-level and protein-level
  diseases. Improving specificity and reducing false detections
  is the primary goal for upcoming versions.
